\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Witnessed source-update calculation, showing the two initial \(A=0\) assertions. The unchanged \(A=1\) groups have weights one and four. The bottom path denotes the \((0,0)\) \emph  {correction} only. Addition of batch 02 and retraction of old batch 01 instead use root \(\to A=0\to (0,1)\). Root mass times suffix message gives the joint event, which is divided by the conditioning mass. Each operation revises the supported calculation.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:updates}{{3}{5}{Witnessed source-update calculation, showing the two initial \(A=0\) assertions. The unchanged \(A=1\) groups have weights one and four. The bottom path denotes the \((0,0)\) \emph {correction} only. Addition of batch 02 and retraction of old batch 01 instead use root \(\to A=0\to (0,1)\). Root mass times suffix message gives the joint event, which is divided by the conditioning mass. Each operation revises the supported calculation}{figure.3}{}}
