\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Warm full-API latency on the even-parity family. Only the latency panels are shown: (a) one query, (b) 1024 queries. Points are medians of per-regime median timings, and shading spans the minimum to maximum across fixed-coordinate counts and locations. Each regime has two warmups and eleven synchronised samples. Direct methods scan packed rows or weighted unique rows, which have equal support size here. The blue curve, labelled ``exact recursive''\ in the saved plot, evaluates continuations by backwards integer messages, with width two. These are observations on the recorded 4 GB GPU, not hardware-independent latencies. The complete diagnostic figure and protocol appear in Supporting Information~\ref {app:dm-timings}.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:locality}{{4}{7}{Warm full-API latency on the even-parity family. Only the latency panels are shown: (a) one query, (b) 1024 queries. Points are medians of per-regime median timings, and shading spans the minimum to maximum across fixed-coordinate counts and locations. Each regime has two warmups and eleven synchronised samples. Direct methods scan packed rows or weighted unique rows, which have equal support size here. The blue curve, labelled \lq \lq exact recursive\rq \rq \ in the saved plot, evaluates continuations by backwards integer messages, with width two. These are observations on the recorded 4 GB GPU, not hardware-independent latencies. The complete diagnostic figure and protocol appear in Supporting Information~\ref {app:dm-timings}}{figure.4}{}}
