\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Complete structured-query diagnostic. (a,b) The parity latency panels used in the main paper. (c) Query support fraction as the number \(r\) of fixed coordinates changes, for \(D=13,\ldots  ,19\). (d) For \(D=19,Q=1024\), quotient storage, integer plan, query workspace and estimated logical reads are different costs. The last bar is an algorithmic byte-load estimate, not measured DRAM traffic. (e) Separate control laws, not the parity family: a repeated 64-world support favours weighted direct evaluation, while high-entropy unique support exceeds the continuation kernel's width capacity. The resource labels appear below (d), and the method legend beside (e). ``Exact recursive''\ in the saved plot means exact continuation evaluation by the integer messages above. Orange circles denote raw packed scanning, green squares weighted-unique scanning and blue triangles continuation evaluation in (a,b). The same method colours apply to (e), whose blue cross is a refusal, not a timing.}}{15}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dm-all-timings}{{6}{15}{Complete structured-query diagnostic. (a,b) The parity latency panels used in the main paper. (c) Query support fraction as the number \(r\) of fixed coordinates changes, for \(D=13,\ldots ,19\). (d) For \(D=19,Q=1024\), quotient storage, integer plan, query workspace and estimated logical reads are different costs. The last bar is an algorithmic byte-load estimate, not measured DRAM traffic. (e) Separate control laws, not the parity family: a repeated 64-world support favours weighted direct evaluation, while high-entropy unique support exceeds the continuation kernel's width capacity. The resource labels appear below (d), and the method legend beside (e). \lq \lq Exact recursive\rq \rq \ in the saved plot means exact continuation evaluation by the integer messages above. Orange circles denote raw packed scanning, green squares weighted-unique scanning and blue triangles continuation evaluation in (a,b). The same method colours apply to (e), whose blue cross is a refusal, not a timing}{figure.6}{}}
