\newlabel{fig:dm-frames}{{8}{20}{FRAMES endpoint comparison. Lexical-proxy success and judged correctness answer different questions. Both retrieval routes have the same 8k initial allowance and at most one missing-needs-triggered 4k delivery. The final judged difference is one answer on 190 questions, not evidence that the methods are equivalent}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Completed shared-index LongMem comparison. Answer correctness includes all 48 questions and six abstentions. Complete required-turn coverage uses 42 positive-evidence questions. The saved ``Relational retrieval''\ and dense series are the shared-dense \texttt  {ours\_keys} and \texttt  {dense\_keys} arms defined above. They invoke the same score call and packer, not different exact readout implementations. Evidence-context allowances are 4000 and 8000 tokens.}}{20}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dm-longmem}{{9}{20}{Completed shared-index LongMem comparison. Answer correctness includes all 48 questions and six abstentions. Complete required-turn coverage uses 42 positive-evidence questions. The saved \lq \lq Relational retrieval\rq \rq \ and dense series are the shared-dense \texttt {ours\_keys} and \texttt {dense\_keys} arms defined above. They invoke the same score call and packer, not different exact readout implementations. Evidence-context allowances are 4000 and 8000 tokens}{figure.9}{}}
